<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>io.github.martinlong1978.FluutCAM</id>
  <name>FluutCAM</name>
  <summary>Open-source CAM for CNC milling</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.martinlong1978">
    <name>Martin Long</name>
  </developer>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>MIT OR Apache-2.0</project_license>
  <description>
    <p>
      FluutCAM turns a 3-D or 2-D model into G-code for a CNC mill. Import a STEP, DXF, SVG or
      STL model, describe the stock and the work zero in a Setup, add toolpaths, check them in the
      simulation and post G-code for your machine.
    </p>
    <p>
      It supports 3-axis, rotary and indexed Setups, 2-D and 3-D toolpath types, and a command
      line program, fluut, for batch work. FluutCAM has no account, no telemetry and no
      advertising. Your files stay on your computer.
    </p>
    <p>
      This Flatpak has no network access and no file access beyond the files you choose in the
      file dialogs.
    </p>
  </description>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.martinlong1978.FluutCAM.desktop</launchable>
  <provides>
    <binary>fluutcam</binary>
    <binary>fluut</binary>
  </provides>
